# Personal working documents — never project documentation.
#
# Repo audits, skill assessments, resume and interview notes, and anything
# else written ABOUT the author rather than about the software. These get
# generated in-tree by habit and must not be published with it.
RESUME*
*RESUME*
*-AUDIT.md
*-audit.md
AUDIT*.md
*ASSESSMENT*
*assessment*
*SKILL-*.md
INTERVIEW*
*interview-notes*
LINKEDIN*
*linkedin*
CV.md
CV-*.md
notes.md
NOTES.md
private/
personal/

# Admin screenshots that capture an issued password.
#
# `/admin/users` shows a generated password exactly once, in plaintext, so any
# capture of that panel is a live credential in a public repository. The
# create-user and reset-password flows are the two that do it.
#
# Scoped to this directory only — `*` does not cross `/`, so the tracked
# docs/screenshots/failures/wrong-password.png (a rejected-login state, no
# secret in it) is deliberately unaffected.
docs/screenshots/*password*.png

# Regenerated by `npm run verify:pages` on every run — 19MB of full-page
# renders at three widths. The suite is the artefact; these are its output.
docs/screenshots/pages/
